---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout>
    <section class="mt-2 relative h-42 md:h-80 border border-white/50 flex flex-col justify-center bg-[#202020] overflow-hidden">
        <img
            src="/images/doodles/core-rules.png"
            alt="A cat holding a paper."
            class="absolute right-2 bottom-2 h-28 md:h-60 opacity-20"
        />

        <div class="ml-6 md:ml-10 w-4/5 md:w-fit z-10">
            <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Artwork Usage Policy</h1>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm md:text-base text-white/70">
                Rules and permissions regarding the use of my artworks.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-2 border border-white/50 p-6 md:p-10">
        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
            My artworks are shared across this website and other platforms. If
            you'd like to use any of them, please follow the guidelines below.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-white/40">
            Policy last updated: November 14th, 2026. These guidelines may
            change over time, so please check this page for updates.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-cyan-400">Allowed</h2>

                <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-white/70 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
                    <li>
                        Personal use, including wallpapers, profile pictures,
                        and banners. Watermarks may only be removed when the
                        artwork is kept private.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Reposting or sharing my non-commissioned artworks
                        publicly, provided proper credit is given and the
                        watermark remains intact.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Sharing screenshots of my artworks with proper credit.
                        An accidentally cropped or missing watermark is
                        acceptable in this case.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Creating fanart or original works inspired by my
                        artworks, provided they are independently created and do
                        not trace or copy my work. Credit is optional.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Commissioners may publish, edit, use commercially, and
                        share their commissioned artwork files without asking
                        for additional permission. Credit is appreciated but
                        optional.
                    </li>
                    <li>Cropping my non-commissioned artworks.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-400">Prohibited</h2>

                <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-white/70 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
                    <li>
                        Using my artworks in inappropriate, harmful, offensive,
                        or misleading contexts.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Using my artworks for AI training, fine-tuning, testing,
                        dataset creation, or analysis.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Uploading my artworks to AI tools as inputs or
                        references, including image-to-image generation, image
                        description, or other AI-generated derivatives.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Tracing, directly reproducing, or copying my artworks.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Editing non-commissioned artworks, including adding
                        text, applying filters, recoloring, or making other
                        alterations. Cropping is allowed.
                    </li>
                    <li>Removing watermarks from artworks shared publicly.</li>
                    <li>
                        Redistributing original non-commissioned artwork files
                        through file-sharing services, external file hosts, or
                        other platforms.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-yellow-200">
                    Requires Permission
                </h2>

                <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-white/70 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
                    <li>
                        Using non-commissioned artworks in commercial content,
                        including monetized videos, advertisements, or
                        promotional material for businesses, products, or
                        services.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Using non-commissioned artworks in personal projects,
                        such as personal websites, free games, school projects,
                        or hobby projects.
                    </li>
                    <li>Any use not explicitly covered by this policy.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 mt-8 border-t border-white/30 flex flex-col gap-3">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-white/50 text-xs">
                <span class="material-symbols-sharp text-xl">info</span>
                <p class="mt-1">
                    Permission must be explicitly granted before proceeding.
                    Giving credit does not replace the need for permission. For
                    public reposts, credit me as&nbsp;
                    <span class="text-white/70">
                        Artwork by @core5570r (Instagram)
                    </span>
                    .
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</MainLayout>
